Q: Bind an entire control instead of individual properties in C# WPF .NET 8 A: <p>If you have multiple text-fields with different background colors you can use a custom user control that binds to a view model object. Something like:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;UserControl x:Class=&quot;MyProject.ColoredTextboxView&quot;
             xmlns=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation&quot;
             xmlns:x=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml&quot;
             xmlns:mc=&quot;http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006&quot; 
             xmlns:d=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008&quot; 
             xmlns:local=&quot;clr-namespace:MyProject.Views&quot;
             mc:Ignorable=&quot;d&quot; 
             d:DesignHeight=&quot;450&quot; d:DesignWidth=&quot;800&quot;&gt;
    &lt;TextBlock Text=&quot;{Binding Text}&quot; Background=&quot;{Binding Background}&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/UserControl&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>And used like this in your MainView</p>
<pre><code>&lt;ColoredTextboxView DataContext=&quot;{Binding MyTextViewModel}&quot;/&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>With a corresponding view model</p>
<pre><code>public class ColoredTextboxViewModel : INotifyPropertyChanged
{
    public string Text
    {
        get;
        set =&gt; SetField(ref field, value);
    }
    public Brush Background
    {
        get;
        set =&gt; SetField(ref field, value);
    }
    public event PropertyChangedEventHandler PropertyChanged;
    protected virtual void OnPropertyChanged([CallerMemberName] string propertyName = null)
    {
        PropertyChanged?.Invoke(this, new PropertyChangedEventArgs(propertyName));
    }
    protected bool SetField&lt;T&gt;(ref T field, T value, [CallerMemberName] string propertyName = null)
    {
        if (EqualityComparer&lt;T&gt;.Default.Equals(field, value)) return false;
        field = value;
        OnPropertyChanged(propertyName);
        return true;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>and used in your MainViewModel like</p>
<pre><code>public ColoredTextboxViewModel MyTextViewModel {get;} = new ();
...
MyTextViewModel.Text = &quot;test&quot;;
MyTextViewModel.Background = Brushes.White;
</code></pre>
<p>A custom control like this is mostly useful if you have commonly used UI elements that you want to reuse. If you just have a single text field there is not really a better solution that binding each property you want to change. But there are some features in WPF that can reduce the need of properties in your view model.</p>
<ol>
<li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/desktop/wpf/controls/styles-templates-overview" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Styles</a> can be used to set property values for all controls of a specific type.</li>
<li><a href="https://wpf-tutorial.com/styles/trigger-datatrigger-event-trigger/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Triggers</a> can be used to change property values based on something else. A typical example is mouse over effects.</li>
<li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/desktop/wpf/advanced/typeconverters-and-xaml" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Type converters</a> can be used for converting a property in the viewModel to the correct type for the corresponding view-property or vice versa. So you could write something like <code>Background=&quot;{Binding Text, Converter={StaticResource EmptyStringToRedConverter}}&quot;</code> to show a red background if the text is empty. See also <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/desktop/wpf/data/how-to-implement-binding-validation" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Binding Validation</a></li>
</ol>
<p>This patter is called Model-View-ViewModel (MVVM). In your own answer you just implement all logic as &quot;code behind&quot;. This is fine, but if you are learning I would recommend taking some time to implement the same thing using MVVM. This pattern is fairly common, so it is almost inevitable that you will need to learn it. There are some tools that can help with MVVM, like <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/communitytoolkit/mvvm/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">MVVMToolkit</a>. These can simplify the syntax quite a bit, but it is still useful to learn the basics if you ever need to work on code that does not use these tools.</p>
<p>If you think the xaml syntax is verbose and difficult to learn and understand, that is unfortunately a downside with WPF. Reading articles and tutorials will help, but I still struggle once I get into the more advanced stuff like controlTemplates.</p>

Q: Symfony request object doesn&#39;t return any query or request (GET or POST) parameters A: <p>More detailed information about my comment.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Symfony 7.4</p>
</li>
<li><p>PHP 8.2</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Possible problem 1.</strong></p>
<p>The .htaccess should contain the following :</p>
<pre><code>&lt;IfModule mod_rewrite.c&gt;
    RewriteEngine On

# If the requested path is not a file or a directory, then redirect everything to index.php
    RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-f
    RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d
    RewriteRule ^(.*)$ index.php [QSA,L]
&lt;/IfModule&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>After  <code>sudo systemctl restart apache2</code></p>
<p><strong>Possible problem 2.</strong></p>
<p>Symfony routing ignores the parameters.</p>
<p>All parameters (in the URL) are available via the query property of the Request object. This is a ParameterBag.</p>
<p><code>$request-&gt;query</code> - GET‑parameters</p>
<p><code>$request-&gt;request</code> - POST‑parameters (<code>POST</code> or <code>application/x-www-form-urlencoded</code> or <code>multipart/form-data</code>)</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Request;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Response;

private RequestStack $requestStack;

public function __construct(RequestStack $requestStack)
{
    $this-&gt;requestStack = $requestStack;
}

$request = $this-&gt;requestStack-&gt;getCurrentRequest();

$expires = $request-&gt;query-&gt;get('expires');
$signature = $request-&gt;query-&gt;get('signature');
$token = $request-&gt;query-&gt;get('token');

$locale = $request-&gt;query-&gt;get('locale', en'); // if necessary

// Verify
if ($request-&gt;query-&gt;has('token') || !$token) {...}

// Сan get all the parameters as an array
$allParams = $request-&gt;query-&gt;all();
</code></pre>
